<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Dun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">266–324</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Dun was a general of the Eastern Jin dynasty from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-clan-of-langya">Wang clan of Langya</a> and a cousin of the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-dao">Wang Dao</a>. As governor of Jing province on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> he commanded the strongest army of the new dynasty. In 322 he rebelled against Emperor Yuan and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jiankang</a>, and in 324 he rose again against Emperor Ming but died of illness during the campaign, after which his forces were defeated.</p></div>
